# Go packages blocked from auto-upgrade (require manual migration).
#
# Format: module/path  # BLOCKER: <substantive reason>
#
# The BLOCKER convention is enforced by .ci/scripts/quality/check-go-deps.sh
# (see parse_blockered_list in .ci/scripts/lib/blocker-validator.sh): each
# line needs a 30+ char reason that does not match the banned-phrase list.
#
# Minor/patch updates for non-blocked packages will fail CI. Major updates
# are always reported but never auto-upgraded regardless of this list.

# Docker SDK — RE-REVIEWED 2026-09-04 by running the upgrade, and the previous reason
# was half wrong. It claimed "v26+ breaks client.NewClientWithOpts signature ... requires
# rewrite of renet docker client". Measured against v28.5.2+incompatible with
# go-connections v0.8.1: NewClientWithOpts, WithHost, WithAPIVersionNegotiation, Close,
# Info, ContainerList(ctx, container.ListOptions{}) and ContainerStats all compile
# unchanged. There is no client rewrite in this.
#
# What DOES break is seven call sites in three files, all of them type RENAMES:
#   pkg/stats/stats.go:39,105        types.StatsJSON
#   pkg/hub/containers.go:40,41,392,404  types.ExecConfig, types.ExecStartCheck
#   pkg/hub/audit.go:84              types.EventsOptions
# each moved out of api/types into api/types/container and api/types/events.
github.com/docker/docker  # BLOCKER: v28 moves seven types renet uses out of api/types (StatsJSON, ExecConfig, ExecStartCheck, EventsOptions); the edit is small but it changes what renet sends to a live daemon, so it lands with an E2E run behind it rather than beside an unrelated PR
github.com/docker/go-connections  # BLOCKER: v0.8.1 builds fine on its own, but it is only reachable together with docker/docker v28 above; unpinning it alone leaves v25 without sockets.DialPipe, so the two move as one

# go-landlock — sandbox isolation primitive (security-critical)
github.com/landlock-lsm/go-landlock  # BLOCKER: v0.9.0 is a 0.x minor that can change the Landlock config API; this gates repo-sandbox isolation, so adoption needs sandbox-behavior validation on a live cluster before bumping

# BLOCKER: kubelet is consumed for exactly one thing, the stable pluginregistration/v1
